1
00:00:00,400 --> 00:00:03,301
你在分诊聊天里只打了一个词：你好
You typed one word into the triage chat: hello.

2
00:00:03,467 --> 00:00:05,195
回来的却是三样东西
And three things came back.

3
00:00:05,195 --> 00:00:10,891
给你的一句问候；一段写给在中国的家长的摘要；还有一张折起来的收据
A greeting for you. A summary written for a parent in China. And, folded away, a receipt:

4
00:00:10,891 --> 00:00:16,907
思考了 3 秒、依据、检查通过、判断，还有模型和价钱
thought for three seconds, sources, a check that passed, a judgment, and a model with a price.

5
00:00:17,067 --> 00:00:22,486
可这个应用建在 OpenAI 的 API 上，而一次 API 调用只会返回一段文字
But the app is built on the OpenAI API, and an API call returns text.

6
00:00:22,806 --> 00:00:24,832
没人要过家长摘要
Nobody asked for a parent summary.

7
00:00:25,152 --> 00:00:27,115
那是谁决定要有这一段的？
So who decided there would be one?

8
00:00:27,435 --> 00:00:29,235
又是谁检查过它？
And who checked it?

9
00:00:32,400 --> 00:00:34,600
我们心里通常是这样一张图
Here is the picture most of us carry:

10
00:00:34,600 --> 00:00:38,821
页面把你的话发给模型，模型再把话发回来
the page sends your words to the model, and the model sends words back.

11
00:00:39,000 --> 00:00:45,104
实际上，页面只和我们自己的一个小服务器说话，再由服务器去调模型
Here is what really happens. The page talks only to our own small server, and the server talks

12
00:00:45,104 --> 00:00:47,896
API key 只放在服务器上
to the model. The API key lives only there.

13
00:00:48,067 --> 00:00:51,203
包在模型调用外面的这层代码，叫 harness
The code wrapped around a model call is called a harness.

14
00:00:51,523 --> 00:00:56,831
我们的 harness 干四件事：组装请求、规定回答的格式、检查回答
Ours does four jobs: build the request, set the shape of the reply, check the reply,

15
00:00:56,831 --> 00:00:59,928
最后回到页面上，把回答变成你看到的样子
and, back in the page, turn it into what you saw.

16
00:01:03,667 --> 00:01:05,302
先看请求
Start with the request.

17
00:01:05,352 --> 00:01:07,422
你的「你好」是里面最小的一块
Your hello is the smallest part of it.

18
00:01:07,600 --> 00:01:14,258
最上面是学校医疗中心和学生保险的 15 份官方资料
On top sit 15 official pages from the university's health service and its student insurance,

19
00:01:14,258 --> 00:01:20,699
清洗成纯文字，大约 25,000 个 token
cleaned into plain text: about 25,000 tokens, the word pieces a model reads and bills by.

20
00:01:21,019 --> 00:01:22,750
token 是模型读字、算钱的单位；这些加起来，相当于一本小册子
A small booklet.

21
00:01:22,800 --> 00:01:25,829
下面是事实卡里 89 条核对过的事实
Below them, 89 checked facts from our fact cards:

22
00:01:25,829 --> 00:01:28,487
每个电话、每个金额、每段营业时间
every phone number, price and opening hour.

23
00:01:28,807 --> 00:01:32,988
每张卡都引用了原文里的那一句，但发给模型的只有事实本身
Each card quotes the sentence it came from; the model gets just the fact.

24
00:01:33,167 --> 00:01:38,479
然后是规则，用大白话写：不诊断，不给剂量
Then the rules, in plain language. Never diagnose. Never give a dose.

25
00:01:38,479 --> 00:01:45,178
紧急时先行动、后谈钱；还有，家长在中国拨 911 打不到波士顿
In an emergency, action before money. And a parent in China cannot dial 911 for Boston.

26
00:01:45,334 --> 00:01:48,662
最后是回答必须填的那张表的说明
Last comes a description of the form the answer must fill.

27
00:01:48,982 --> 00:01:53,846
这四块合起来叫 instructions，聊天应用里叫系统提示词
Together, these four parts are the instructions; chat apps call them the system prompt.

28
00:01:54,000 --> 00:01:56,328
它们每次都一样，这一点很要紧
They never change, and that matters.

29
00:01:56,328 --> 00:02:02,860
OpenAI 的缓存从请求的第一个字开始比对，所以不变的东西必须放在最前面
OpenAI's cache matches a request from its very first word, so whatever never changes must come first.

30
00:02:02,860 --> 00:02:06,405
第一次之后，前面这一大段就直接从缓存里读
After the first call, the long top is read from the cache.

31
00:02:06,405 --> 00:02:08,099
这叫 prompt caching，提示缓存
This is prompt caching,

32
00:02:08,099 --> 00:02:12,368
在 Luna 模型上，命中缓存的 token 只要原价的十分之一
and on the Luna model a cached token costs a tenth of a fresh one.

33
00:02:12,534 --> 00:02:13,915
后面才是会变的
Then what changes:

34
00:02:13,915 --> 00:02:19,972
前面聊过的话、谁在问、波士顿和中国此刻几点、学校医疗中心开没开门
the chat so far, who is asking, the time in Boston and in China, whether the student clinic is open,

35
00:02:19,972 --> 00:02:21,584
最后才是那句「你好」
and finally, hello.

36
00:02:21,634 --> 00:02:25,452
你的一句「你好」带着整本小册子出发，只花了 0.0004 美元
Your hello carried the whole booklet, and cost four hundredths of a cent.

37
00:02:25,600 --> 00:02:30,642
停一下：为什么要由我们的代码告诉模型现在几点、诊所开没开门
Pause here. Why does our code tell the model the time, and whether the clinic is open,

38
00:02:30,642 --> 00:02:33,046
而不是让模型自己去算？
instead of letting the model work it out?

39
00:02:37,700 --> 00:02:39,513
因为模型没有钟
Because a model has no clock.

40
00:02:39,833 --> 00:02:44,818
代码查公布的营业时间和时区，每次都用同一套算法
Code reads the posted hours and the time zone, works it out the same way every time,

41
00:02:44,818 --> 00:02:47,727
算不准的时候，就写「待确认」
and writes 'to be confirmed' when it cannot know.

42
00:02:53,267 --> 00:02:59,006
接下来是回答的格式。 我们不是请模型「回答」，而是递给它一张表
Next, the shape of the reply. We do not ask the model for an answer. We hand it a form.

43
00:02:59,167 --> 00:03:01,947
13 个格子，每个都有名字和类型
13 boxes, each with a name and a type.

44
00:03:01,947 --> 00:03:03,410
有的填自由文字
Some take free text.

45
00:03:03,410 --> 00:03:05,531
有的只能从固定选项里选
Some take only fixed choices:

46
00:03:05,531 --> 00:03:07,653
紧急程度只能是六档之一
urgency is one of six levels,

47
00:03:07,653 --> 00:03:12,116
从「可能危及生命」一直到「只是规则或保险问题」
from possibly life-threatening down to just a rules question.

48
00:03:12,267 --> 00:03:14,783
API 里这叫 structured outputs，结构化输出
The API calls this structured outputs.

49
00:03:14,998 --> 00:03:19,947
它仍然是一次调用，回来的仍然是文字，只是文字长成了这张表的样子
It is still one call, and the reply is still text, just text shaped like the form.

50
00:03:20,267 --> 00:03:24,576
开了严格模式，别的样子都不行：不能少一格，也不能多一格
In strict mode nothing else fits: no missing box, no extra box.

51
00:03:24,734 --> 00:03:27,285
现在看其中一格：家长摘要
Now look at one box: the parent summary.

52
00:03:27,285 --> 00:03:32,451
规则给了它一条说明：写给在中国的家长两三句话
The rules give it an instruction: two or three sentences for the parent in China.

53
00:03:32,451 --> 00:03:35,958
孩子怎么了、要去哪里、家长能做什么
What is happening, where to go, what the parent can do.

54
00:03:35,958 --> 00:03:37,150
永远要写
Always filled in.

55
00:03:37,200 --> 00:03:43,131
秘密就这么多：一次调用填满全部 13 格，家长摘要也在其中
That is the whole secret: one call fills all 13 boxes, the parent summary included.

56
00:03:43,451 --> 00:03:47,589
不是模型自己想得周到，而是规则说这一格必须填
The model did not decide to be thoughtful; the rules say fill that box.

57
00:03:47,909 --> 00:03:52,575
严格模式只保证这一格存在，不保证里面有字
And strict mode only promises the box is there, not that anything is in it,

58
00:03:52,575 --> 00:03:54,566
所以空着交上来，检查就不让过
so the checker rejects it empty.

59
00:03:54,734 --> 00:03:58,981
收据也一样：「依据」就是 citations 那一格
The receipt works the same way. Sources is the citations box.

60
00:03:58,981 --> 00:04:03,438
「判断」就是紧急程度和该去哪里这两格，翻成了中文
Judgment is the urgency and where-to-go boxes, put into Chinese.

61
00:04:10,900 --> 00:04:13,396
填好的表还不会直接上屏
The filled form does not go to the screen yet.

62
00:04:13,716 --> 00:04:15,815
先要过我们自己写的一道检查
First it passes a checker we wrote,

63
00:04:15,815 --> 00:04:19,412
叫 lint，名字借自给代码挑错的工具
called the lint, after the tools that flag mistakes in code.

64
00:04:19,567 --> 00:04:22,444
二十多条规则逐句读
More than twenty rules read every line.

65
00:04:22,444 --> 00:04:26,205
拦下剂量，比如「每六小时两片」
They stop a dose, like two tablets every six hours.

66
00:04:26,205 --> 00:04:30,705
拦下诊断；拦下不在任何事实卡上的电话和金额
A diagnosis. A phone number or price that is on no fact card.

67
00:04:30,705 --> 00:04:33,139
拦下紧急时先谈钱
Money before 911 in an emergency.

68
00:04:33,139 --> 00:04:35,204
也拦下空着的家长摘要
And an empty parent summary.

69
00:04:35,767 --> 00:04:38,843
有不通过的，表就被退回去，附一张条子
If anything fails, the form goes back with a note:

70
00:04:38,843 --> 00:04:41,612
改掉这几处，重新交一份完整的表
fix these problems and return the whole form.

71
00:04:41,932 --> 00:04:43,483
只给一次重写机会
One rewrite, no more.

72
00:04:43,533 --> 00:04:49,102
第二版还不过，或者调用出错了，模型写的字一个都不给人看
If the second version still fails, or the call breaks, nobody sees the model's words.

73
00:04:49,102 --> 00:04:52,181
换成我们自己写好的兜底
A fallback we wrote ourselves goes out instead:

74
00:04:52,181 --> 00:04:56,440
紧急就现在打 911，不紧急就打学校医疗中心
call 911 now if it was urgent, otherwise call the student clinic.

75
00:04:56,600 --> 00:05:01,805
还有，只要有一版说了紧急，重写和兜底都只能还是紧急
And once any version says emergency, the rewrite and the fallback must stay emergency.

76
00:05:02,125 --> 00:05:06,605
重写只该改掉检查挑出的毛病，不该改变对危险的判断
A rewrite should fix what the checker flagged, not change its mind about danger.

77
00:05:06,925 --> 00:05:10,488
真要错，宁可错在打 911 这一边
If we must be wrong, we would rather be wrong toward 911.

78
00:05:10,667 --> 00:05:15,488
可规则里已经告诉过模型「不要诊断」了，为什么还要再查一遍？
But the rules already told the model never to diagnose. Why check again?

79
00:05:20,167 --> 00:05:23,175
因为指令只是请求，不是保证
Because an instruction is a request, not a guarantee.

80
00:05:23,495 --> 00:05:27,058
收据上的「检查」那一行，写的就是这条回答走了哪条路
The check row on your receipt says which path the answer took:

81
00:05:27,058 --> 00:05:29,127
一次通过、重写过一次，还是被换掉了
passed, rewritten once, or replaced.

82
00:05:31,967 --> 00:05:36,276
只有检查过的表才会到页面上，页面再把它排成聊天的样子
Only a checked form reaches the page, and the page lays it out like a chat.

83
00:05:36,434 --> 00:05:38,685
紧急的步骤排最前面，放在红框里
Urgent steps first, in a red block.

84
00:05:38,685 --> 00:05:44,089
然后是说明、去处、要带什么、可以照着说的英文句子
Then the explanation, the places to go, what to bring, a sentence to say in English,

85
00:05:44,089 --> 00:05:48,978
最后是折起来的家长摘要，学生还有一个复制按钮
and near the end the folded parent summary, with a copy button for students.

86
00:05:49,134 --> 00:05:50,334
那张收据呢？
And the receipt?

87
00:05:50,334 --> 00:05:52,734
「依据」和「判断」来自表
Sources and judgment come from the form.

88
00:05:52,734 --> 00:05:54,599
「检查」来自检查器
Check comes from the checker.

89
00:05:54,599 --> 00:05:58,200
「模型」和价钱来自服务器和它的价目表
Model and price come from the server and its price list.

90
00:05:58,367 --> 00:06:00,949
那「过程」呢？ Luna 是推理模型
And process? Luna is a reasoning model.

91
00:06:00,949 --> 00:06:07,239
动笔之前，它先在看不见的地方一步步推理，这部分我们付了钱，却看不到
Before writing a word, it reasons in hidden steps that we pay for but never see, and the effort

92
00:06:07,239 --> 00:06:09,490
菜单里的思考强度，决定它想多少
setting in the menu says how much.

93
00:06:09,490 --> 00:06:14,721
页面给每一段计时：第一个字到来之前算「思考」，之后算「写」
The page times each phase: thinking until the first word arrives, then writing.

94
00:06:14,721 --> 00:06:18,826
所以思考是真的；它想了些什么，下一集讲
So the thinking is real. What it contains is the next episode.

95
00:06:19,000 --> 00:06:21,000
想一想：五行里有两行是模型自己写的
Now a question to sit with.

96
00:06:21,050 --> 00:06:23,608
检查器会读其中一行
Two of the five rows are the model's own words.

97
00:06:23,928 --> 00:06:25,728
另一行，从来没有任何东西检查它
The checker reads one of them.

98
00:06:25,955 --> 00:06:27,755
是哪一行？
Which one does nothing ever check?

99
00:06:32,100 --> 00:06:37,107
是「依据」。 检查器会读「判断」，确保紧急情况排在最前
Sources. The checker reads the judgment to make sure an emergency comes first,

100
00:06:37,107 --> 00:06:41,280
也会拿事实卡核对每个电话和金额
and it tests every phone number and price against the fact cards.

101
00:06:41,280 --> 00:06:46,159
但没有任何东西读依据列表，那只是模型自己说它参考了什么
But nothing reads the source list. It is simply what the model says it used.

102
00:06:49,267 --> 00:06:51,699
这套设计不是一开始的样子
This design is not where the work started.

103
00:06:52,019 --> 00:06:57,459
背后那个 PR 前后 36 个小时、60 个提交，是用 Claude Code 写出来的
The pull request behind it ran 36 hours and 60 commits, written with Claude Code.

104
00:06:57,634 --> 00:07:03,896
周二先做的是知识库，结果发现资料之间互相打架
On Tuesday, the knowledge base came first, and the sources turned out to disagree.

105
00:07:03,896 --> 00:07:10,693
一份保险文件说自付上限是 5,550 美元，另一份说 5,500
One insurance document puts the out-of-pocket maximum at 5,550 dollars, another at 5,500.

106
00:07:10,693 --> 00:07:15,810
七处这样的冲突被逐条裁定，或者标成「待确认」
Seven conflicts like that were ruled on, or marked to be confirmed.

107
00:07:15,967 --> 00:07:21,621
第一版引擎是规则：代码按关键词表判断症状有多急
The first engine was rules: code judged how urgent a symptom was from keyword lists,

108
00:07:21,621 --> 00:07:25,055
模型只负责抽取信息、把结果讲清楚
and the model only extracted details and explained.

109
00:07:25,375 --> 00:07:28,878
还搭了一套评估，准备比较六种做法
We also built an evaluation to compare six approaches,

110
00:07:28,878 --> 00:07:31,604
但在真正比较之前就暂停了
then shelved it before the comparison ran.

111
00:07:31,767 --> 00:07:34,924
然后，周二晚上九点二十一分，转向
Then, at nine twenty-one on Tuesday night, the turn.

112
00:07:35,244 --> 00:07:39,810
关键词表一边漏掉真正的危险信号，一边误报无害的说法
The keyword lists kept missing real warning signs and flagging harmless ones.

113
00:07:40,130 --> 00:07:45,144
于是你决定：让推理模型带着整本资料自己判断
So you decided: let a reasoning model judge, with the whole booklet in front of it,

114
00:07:45,144 --> 00:07:48,044
把对输出的检查当作唯一的安全层
and make the output check the only safety layer.

115
00:07:48,200 --> 00:07:51,528
二十二分钟后，一个最朴素的聊天框就有了
Twenty-two minutes later, the plainest chat box existed.

116
00:07:51,848 --> 00:07:53,475
之后又有四十个提交
Forty more commits followed,

117
00:07:53,475 --> 00:07:57,544
大部分都在堵坏句子溜过检查的路
most of them closing a way a bad sentence could slip past the checker.

118
00:07:57,700 --> 00:08:01,664
注意这里的反转：判断症状时，词语规则被放弃了
Notice the twist: word rules were dropped for judging symptoms,

119
00:08:01,664 --> 00:08:06,383
可安全网仍然是词语规则，只是对准了模型写的句子
yet the safety net is still word rules, now aimed at the model's sentences.

120
00:08:06,703 --> 00:08:08,687
这个取舍，留到第四集
That trade-off is episode four.

121
00:08:16,933 --> 00:08:20,338
从外面看，它很像 ChatGPT 或 Claude
From the outside, this looks like ChatGPT or Claude;

122
00:08:20,338 --> 00:08:25,445
样子是有意照着 Claude 的应用做的，那是第三集
the look was borrowed from Claude's app on purpose, and that is episode three.

123
00:08:25,765 --> 00:08:27,792
里面却是另一台机器
Inside, it is a different machine.

124
00:08:27,966 --> 00:08:30,488
通用的聊天应用用自由的文字回答
A general chat app answers in free prose,

125
00:08:30,488 --> 00:08:33,747
靠系统提示词和模型的训练守规矩
guided by its system prompt and the model's training.

126
00:08:34,067 --> 00:08:39,730
我们也有系统提示词，此外还有一张我们设计的表、只从事实卡里取的金额
Ours has a system prompt too, and adds a form we designed, prices only from fact cards,

127
00:08:39,730 --> 00:08:43,049
以及挡在模型和屏幕之间的我们自己的规则
and our own rules between the model and the screen.

128
00:08:43,600 --> 00:08:46,500
这张表也是下一步的钥匙
That form is also the key to what comes next,

129
00:08:46,500 --> 00:08:49,206
因为一个新功能，多半就是多一格
because a new feature is mostly a new box.

130
00:08:49,206 --> 00:08:51,268
一段能转给室友的话
A note to forward to a roommate.

131
00:08:51,268 --> 00:08:53,072
看医生时可以问的问题
Questions to ask the doctor.

132
00:08:53,233 --> 00:08:57,723
每多一格，都要做三件事：表上加一行和它的说明
Each new box needs three things: a line on the form with its instruction,

133
00:08:57,723 --> 00:09:00,614
检查里加一条规则，页面上给它一个位置
a rule in the checker, and a place on the page.

134
00:09:00,934 --> 00:09:03,558
不管哪个 agent 来做，配方都是这三步
That recipe holds whichever agent builds it.

135
00:09:08,533 --> 00:09:10,432
所以：一句「你好」，四件事
So: one hello, four jobs.

136
00:09:10,600 --> 00:09:14,536
组装请求，不变的放前面，好命中缓存
Build the request, unchanging parts first so they are cached.

137
00:09:14,536 --> 00:09:15,633
递一张表
Hand over a form.

138
00:09:15,633 --> 00:09:19,053
逐句检查，给一次重写，备好兜底
Check every line, allow one rewrite, keep a fallback.

139
00:09:19,053 --> 00:09:21,117
最后排成页面，附一张收据
Then lay it out, with a receipt.

140
00:09:21,266 --> 00:09:27,186
三个问题考考自己：请求里哪一部分会被缓存，为什么位置很重要？
Three questions to test yourself. Which part of the request is cached, and why does its position matter?

141
00:09:27,186 --> 00:09:29,862
为什么重写不准收回「紧急」？
Why may a rewrite never take back an emergency?

142
00:09:29,862 --> 00:09:33,106
想加一段「给室友的话」，要改哪几处？
And what would you change to add a note for the roommate?

143
00:09:33,266 --> 00:09:37,155
下一集：「思考了 3 秒」的这几秒里，模型在干什么
Next time: what the model is doing during thought for three seconds,

144
00:09:37,155 --> 00:09:40,242
以及为什么我们给你看的是收据，而不是它的思考
and why we show you a receipt instead of its thoughts.
